<title>GREECE: GREEK MARCH PRIVATE CONSTRUCTION DROPS 10.3PCT Y/Y.</title>
<headline>GREEK MARCH PRIVATE CONSTRUCTION DROPS 10.3PCT Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's index of private</p>
<p>construction activity measured by the construction volume based</p>
<p>on the number of building permits issued fell 10.3 percent</p>
<p>year-on-year in March, the National Statistics Service (NSS)</p>
<p>said.</p>
<p>&quot;In March construction volume based on the number of</p>
<p>building permits nationwide reached 4.115 million cubic metres</p>
<p>against 4.586 million in March 1996, a decrease of 10.3</p>
<p>percent,&quot; NSS said in a statement.</p>
<p>In the three months of the year, private construction</p>
<p>activity was up 1.4 percent compared to the same period a year</p>
<p>ago. Activity in the Attica region decreased 6.0 percent, it</p>
<p>added.</p>
<p>					   March 97    Feb 97    March 97</p>
<p>    Building permits		  5,241	4,888	5,374</p>
<p>    Volume in cubic metres(mln)   4.115	3.993	4.586</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
